    thinking: "**Developing Android App Idea**\n\nI\'m focusing on crafting an Android application to compute LFP battery capacity and watt-hours, factoring in Depth of Discharge settings that the user can adjust. This will mean calculating the usable energy and capacity, given various discharge rates.\n\n\n**Assessing Core Skill Set**\n\nI\'m now taking stock of my skill set to see which areas are most relevant to this project. I\'ve identified several areas, including `frontend-design`, `app-icon-generation`, and `room-database-integration` as potentially crucial. I\'m leaning toward keeping the scope focused to meet the user\'s initial needs, so I will explore `room-database-integration` later.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Design & Persistence**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the app\'s design and local persistence. I intend to deliver a polished, single-screen experience adhering to Material 3 design, complete with visual battery state indicators. The initial approach will lean towards a clean, easy-to-use interface. To increase user value, I\'ve decided to incorporate local persistence of battery configurations and calculation history via Room, aligning with the project goals. I need to review `frontend-design` and `room-database-integration`.\n\n\n"
