    thinking: "**Designing the Application**\n\nI\'m now focusing on designing an application specifically for calculating LFP battery watt-hours and total capacity. My main priority is to incorporate configurable discharge depth settings as a core feature. I\'m aiming for a user-friendly interface that provides accurate and reliable data.\n\n\n**Clarifying Battery Parameters**\n\nI\'m now diving into the specifics of LFP battery characteristics. My focus is on understanding the nominal voltage, fully charged and discharged voltages, and nominal cell capacity (Ah). I\'ve got to ensure the application accurately calculates pack voltage based on series cells and capacity based on parallel cells. I\'m reviewing how the total watt-hours relate to pack voltage and capacity, along with figuring out \"configurable discharge depth settings\".\n\n\n**Calculating Usable Capacity**\n\nI\'m now integrating a dynamic DoD percentage input to calculate usable Ah, Wh, and kWh. I\'m focusing on displaying both total and usable energy, including approximate cycle life, and am thinking of using a lookup or formula for the battery life cycle calculation. I\'m really getting into it now.\n\n\n**Defining Input Specifications**\n\nI\'m now focusing on specific input configurations. I will incorporate both \"Cell & Pack Configuration (S/P)\" and \"Direct Pack Inputs,\" accommodating various setups. I\'m defining cell parameters with preset nominal voltage (3.2V) and capacity values for common DIY LFP cells, and allowing custom inputs. Pack configuration allows series and parallel cell customization, and DoD will be configurable (10-100%).\n\n\n"
