  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing the UI Framework**\n\nI\'ve established the ViewModel, and my focus has shifted towards crafting the UI using Jetpack Compose. I\'m currently pondering the best approach to structure a clean, modern single-screen layout. My goal is to build an eco-friendly user interface.\n\n\n**Visualizing the Gauge**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the UI\'s visual core: the battery gauge. I\'ve decided to leverage `Canvas` for a visually striking horizontal battery cylinder, with a fluid green glow. This will represent the depth of discharge as a percentage of usable energy, offering an intuitive representation. I\'m also exploring an interactive battery cell, dynamically displaying usable kWh, nominal kWh, nominal voltage, and cycles to create a professional feel. My thoughts have moved on to defining the Pack Configuration parameters section that will be next to the battery charge gauge!\n\n\n**Defining Pack Configuration**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the Pack Configuration parameters, specifically the voltage presets: 24V, 36V, and 48V. I\'m keen on a UX-friendly numerical picker for parallel cells and sliders. I will include cell capacity input with preset options like 100 Ah, 200 Ah, and 304 Ah, and also cell voltage input. I am aiming for a seamless and intuitive experience.\n\n\n**Expanding the UI Functionality**\n\nI\'m now integrating new features. I\'m excited about an interactive card displaying \"Usable energy: X.XX kWh\". I\'m also planning a \"Saved Systems / History\" panel for quick saving, loading, and deletion of battery pack configurations, and an \"Appliance Run Time Estimator\" panel. I envision interactive icons for common loads like LED lights and AC units. I\'m focusing on beautiful paddings, Material 3 sliders, elegant rounded cards, dynamic colors, and a clean eco-tech vibe. I think putting it in a main Composable file is extremely straightforward and robust, and will write a file `/app/src/main/java/com/example/ui/Battery.kt`.\n\n\n**Creating the Main File**\n\nI\'m now diving into the implementation phase. I\'ve decided on the file name `BatteryCalculatorScreen.kt` and am committed to building a high-fidelity, polished UI. My top priority is the custom `BatteryGauge` using `Canvas`. I intend to create a visually appealing cylinder that dynamically adjusts its internal fluid level and color based on the Depth of Discharge. I\'ve confirmed we have access to the needed Material 3 extended icons, which will greatly streamline the process and maintain a professional feel.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will create `/app/src/main/java/com/example/ui/BatteryCalculatorScreen.kt` which will house the complete, visually rich interface. It includes a custom battery cylinder gauge drawn using Jetpack Compose `Canvas`, preset chips for cells and voltage systems, interactive sliders, a runtime load simulator for household appliances, and a system save/load manager using our Room history."
