    thinking: "**Considering Offline Expansion**\n\nI\'m focusing on expanding the LFP Battery Calculator app offline, leveraging Room DB and a state-based model. My primary task involves outlining precise, professional, and useful features to enhance the user experience, working within the existing architecture.\n\n\n**Developing Appliance Interface**\n\nI am now developing the interactive device input sector for the app. I\'m focusing on user-friendly selection of appliances, quantities, backup hours, and integrating common wattage and surge data. I will include typical household appliances with their respective wattages and surge currents to ensure accurate calculation of loads. This includes calculating total active load, peak surge load, and starting load.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will check the current contents of `BatteryViewModel.kt` to see how we can expand the state management to support custom appliances, peak surge load calculations, grid selection (On-grid/Off-grid/Hybrid), and auto-cycle calculation based on Cylindrical vs Prismatic LFP cells (15Ah to 314Ah)."
