  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Confirming Perfect Match**\n\nI\'m thrilled! The `strings.xml` file confirms \"LFP Battery Calculator,\" and it\'s perfect. The prompt\'s offline requirement is fully implemented using Jetpack Compose and local SQLite. I\'m pleased with the outcome so far!\n\n\n**Designing Load Selection**\n\nI\'ve made significant progress designing the \"\340\247\247. \340\246\262\340\247\213\340\246\241 \340\246\270\340\246\277\340\246\262\340\247\207\340\246\225\340\246\266\340\246\250\" tab. I\'m focusing on user-friendliness; I\'ve ensured a straightforward input method for common household devices, including LED lights, ceiling fans, smart TVs, Wi-Fi routers, refrigerators, water pumps, air conditioners, and laptop chargers, all of which will be listed.\n\n\n**Refining Power Input**\n\nI\'ve expanded the load selection by incorporating Microwave Ovens and Mobile Chargers. Users can now easily adjust the quantity for each device. Furthermore, I\'ve added a global Target Backup Hours slider (1-24 hours) for specifying backup duration. Now the user can make choices based on their needs. The \"\340\247\251. \340\246\227\340\247\215\340\246\260\340\246\277\340\246\241 \340\246\227\340\246\276\340\246\207\340\246\241 \340\246\223 \340\246\211\340\246\252\340\246\225\340\246\260\340\246\243\" tab now offers Off-grid, On-grid, and Hybrid options.\n\n\n**Detailing Setup & Guides**\n\nI\'m now detailing the \"\340\247\251. \340\246\227\340\247\215\340\246\260\340\246\277\340\246\241 \340\246\227\340\246\276\340\246\207\340\246\241 \340\246\223 \340\246\211\340\246\252\340\246\225\340\246\260\340\246\243\" tab. High-contrast cards will explain the \"\340\246\270\340\247\201\340\246\254\340\246\277\340\246\247\340\246\276\340\246\270\340\246\256\340\247\202\340\246\271\" and \"\340\246\205\340\246\270\340\247\201\340\246\254\340\246\277\340\246\247\340\246\276\340\246\270\340\246\256\340\247\202\340\246\271\" of each grid type (Off-grid, On-grid, Hybrid). I\'m also including a complete list of necessary materials, e.g., solar panels, charge controllers, inverters, DC cables, and DC fuses. I\'m focusing on making the information clear and easy to understand.\n\n\n**Calculating Current Requirements**\n\nI\'m now calculating the exact starting current from the LFP battery pack, considering the system voltage. I will provide tailored setup recommendations, including the minimum pure sine wave inverter size, surge wattage, and DC fuse and cable gauge. For LFP cells, I\'ve defined a list of standard premium cells, from cylindrical to prismatic, 15Ah to 314Ah, along with their selection cycles automatically defined according to their type, and base cycle count, ranging from 2000 cycles to 8000.\n\n\n**Defining Cycle Estimation**\n\nI\'ve defined a system for estimating cycle life that auto-scales based on the cell\'s base cycles and Depth of Discharge. I\'ve curated a list of cells, including both cylindrical and prismatic, from 20Ah to 314Ah, each with a pre-defined cycle count. I\'m excited by how the automated calculations provide users with valuable insights into the longevity of their battery setup. I\'ve double-checked that all the configurations are complete, and confirmed the app passes all checks. I am confident in the readiness for finalizing.\n\n\n**Elaborating Functional Modules**\n\n\340\246\206\340\246\256\340\246\277 \340\246\217\340\246\226\340\246\250 \340\246\225\340\246\276\340\246\260\340\247\215\340\246\257\340\246\225\340\246\260\340\247\200 \340\246\256\340\246\241\340\246\277\340\246\211\340\246\262\340\246\227\340\247\201\340\246\262\340\246\277 \340\246\270\340\246\202\340\246\227\340\246\240\340\246\277\340\246\244 \340\246\225\340\246\260\340\246\233\340\246\277\340\245\244 \340\246\241\340\246\276\340\246\237\340\246\276\340\246\254\340\247\207\340\246\270 \340\246\270\340\246\277\340\246\231\340\247\215\340\246\225\340\247\215\340\246\260\340\247\213\340\246\250\340\246\276\340\246\207\340\246\234\340\247\207