  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing the UI and Persistence**\n\nI\'m currently designing the selection UI, focusing on an intuitive way for users to choose LFP battery types and capacities. I\'m prioritizing automatic linking to cycle life data. Next up, I will work on integrating local data persistence to save selections and calculations, ensuring a smooth user experience even after they close the app.\n\n\n**Reviewing Progress & Features**\n\nI\'ve been reviewing progress, especially the offline data persistence. I\'ve designed the user interface for configuration, and am happy with the four tab structure. Specifically, I\'m verifying the \"Load Selection\", \"Pack Setup\", and \"Grid Guide\" functionalities. Also, the app can calculate LFP battery watt-hours, total capacity, and has configurable discharge depth settings.\n\n\n**Implementing Local Persistence**\n\nI\'m now focused on implementing local data persistence for the active device selection. The goal is to ensure the user\'s current configuration, including device quantities, cell choices, series/parallel arrangements, DoD, backup hours, and grid type, are saved and restored upon app launch. I\'m exploring options like SharedPreferences or Room to persist the `BatteryViewModel`\'s state. I need to make the app \"remember\" the active session. I will review `BatteryViewModel.kt` to plan the integration.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 3
      nanos: 125441203
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
