    thinking: "**Designing Language Selection**\n\nOkay, I\'m exploring the feasibility of a robust, custom language selection system. I\'m leaning towards implementing this within `BatteryViewModel`, or perhaps a dedicated helper object. The goal is a clean mapping of UI text keys to translations, starting with English, Bengali, and Chinese.\n\n\n**Expanding Language Scope**\n\nI\'ve expanded the language list to include German and Korean, along with English, Bengali, and Chinese. Now, I\'m focusing on user-friendliness and app persistence. I need an in-app settings selector for language choice, coupled with a persistence mechanism via `SharedPreferences` within `BatteryViewModel`. A translation helper function, perhaps `t(\"key\")`, is also essential for efficient text lookup.\n\n\n**Refining Language Selection Flow**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on integrating the language selection within the app\'s UI. The plan is a top bar action icon (perhaps using `Icons.Default.Language`) that triggers a bottom sheet or dialog. This will offer immediate access to language choices, including English (default), Bengali (\340\246\254\340\246\276\340\246\202\340\246\262\340\246\276), Chinese (\344\270\255\346\226\207), German (Deutsch), and Korean (\355\225\234\352\265\255\354\226\264). The selection will then trigger a fallback to Bengali/English as needed, with a translation registry for texts on `BatteryCalculatorScreen.kt`. I\'m checking for a settings section to put it into.\n\n\n**Implementing Language Persistence**\n\nI\'ve simplified language persistence considerably. Examining `BatteryViewModel.kt`, I\'m adding an `appLanguage` state variable using `mutableStateOf(\"en\")`. This will be saved/loaded via `SharedPreferences` in `savePreferences()` and `loadPreferences()` respectively, which I\'ve updated. The code now looks robust and easy to deploy.\n\n\n**Creating Localization Helper**\n\nI\'m now focusing on a `BatteryLocalizer` helper class, potentially in `com.example.ui.BatteryLocalizer.kt`, to manage translations. This is to keep `BatteryCalculatorScreen.kt` and `BatteryViewModel.kt` clean. I\'m prioritizing an organized translation dictionary for English, Bengali, Chinese, German, and Korean for all UI texts, particularly labels and headings. I\'ll focus on UI texts, starting with tabs.\n\n\n**Translating UI Elements**\n\nMy current focus is on translating UI texts for the app, beginning with tab names and top bar elements. I\'ve started populating the translation dictionary within `BatteryLocalizer.kt` with English, Bengali, Chinese, German, and Korean equivalents for tab names like \"Load Selection\" and \"Pack Calculator,\" along with top bar elements. The next step will be to handle texts on `BatteryVisualHeader`.\n\n\n**Completing UI Translation**\n\nI\'m translating more UI elements, now including texts on `ApplianceSelectionTab`. This includes labels for \"Cell Used:\", \"Form Factor:\", \"Connected Appliances (Load)\", and descriptions. I\'m also adding translations for units like \"W\" and \"h\", and labels such as \"Total Peak Load (Max)\", \"Total Running Load\", \"Daily Energy Requirement\" and \"Target Backup\". This includes a Bengali translation. I\'ve also covered the texts needed for the tab.\n\n\n**Expanding Translation Scope**\n\nI\'m now expanding the scope of UI text translation, adding Bengali translations alongside English originals for several key elements. I\'ve covered texts such as \"Required Battery Size (with DoD)\", \"Proceed to Setup Pack\", and descriptions for appliances like \"LED Light\", \"DC Fan\", \"Smart LED TV\", \"Inverter Refrigerator\", \"WiFi Router\", \"Laptop Charger\" and \"Mobile Charger\". I\'m also including the title for the pack configuration settings and the instruction for selecting the LFP cell and its capacity. The translation efforts are progressing efficiently.\n\n\n**Adding Translation Components**\n\nI\'m translating more UI elements, including those in the \"Select LFP Cell & Capacity\" section. I\'ve added Bengali translations for descriptions and labels: \"Select LFP Cell & Capacity\", \"Cylindrical\", \"Prismatic\", and the \"Cell Series & Parallel Connections\" section\'s elements such as \"Series Cells (S):\" and \"Parallel Cells (P):\".\n\n\n**Adding Translation Entries**\n\nI\'m now integrating new translation entries into `BatteryLocalizer.kt`, focusing on pack-related analysis and setup screens. I\'ve added Bengali and English translations for labels like \"Pack Total Energy (Wh)\", \"Usable Energy (Wh)\", and \"Peak Surge Load (10 Seconds):\". I also handled descriptions, for elements such as setting the depth of discharge and cell configurations. I added translations for \"Save Design,\" and \"Instant Pack Analysis.\"\n\n\n**Incorporating Solar Translations**\n\nI\'m now incorporating Bengali translations for elements within the `SolarGridGuideTab`. I\'ve added entries for \"Grid Type & Solar Design Guide,\" and various system types like \"Off-Grid,\" \"On-Grid,\" and \"Hybrid.\" I\'ve included translations for labels related to energy requirements and pack lifespans.\n\n\n**Adding Translations**\n\nI\'m translating more texts in `BatteryLocalizer.kt`, now focused on the Solar Grid Guide. I\'m adding Bengali equivalents alongside English for key sections. This includes the labels related to component sizing and material lists: \"Required Materials & Component Sizing,\" \"Required Solar Panel Size,\" and others. My recent updates encompass labels like \"DC Wire Size,\" and \"Pack Fuse Rating,\" to enhance user clarity.\n\n\n\n**Integrating Saved Designs**\n\nI\'m now integrating translations for the saved design section. I\'ve added Bengali and English translations for labels within the `SavedSystemsTab`, including \"No saved designs found,\" \"Save custom designs from...\". I\'ve also incorporated translations for \"Load\" and \"Delete\" buttons, and the save design dialog title and description.\n\n\n"
