  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Translation Logic**\n\nI\'ve begun defining the translation logic within `SolarGridGuideTab`. I\'ve instantiated a translation helper function, which relies on `BatteryLocalizer` and the view model\'s app language. The helper takes a key as input and retrieves the corresponding translated string. Next, I\'ll integrate this helper for specific translations.\n\n\n**Refining Terminology Choices**\n\nI\'m reassessing terminology mapping; \"\340\246\270\340\247\213\340\246\262\340\246\276\340\246\260 \340\246\227\340\247\215\340\246\260\340\246\277\340\246\241 \340\246\205\340\246\252\340\246\266\340\246\250 \340\246\250\340\246\277\340\246\260\340\247\215\340\246\254\340\246\276\340\246\232\340\246\250 \340\246\225\340\246\260\340\247\201\340\246\250\" is better as `t(\"solar_grid_title\")`. For the system descriptions, I\'m leaning toward dynamically localized strings within the component itself. I like the idea of cleaner mapping within the Composable and dynamic localization, especially considering the `viewModel.appLanguage`. I\'m starting the dynamic mapping for `advantagesLabel`.\n\n\n**Localizing UI Elements**\n\nI\'m now implementing dynamic localization for several UI elements. I\'ve defined language-specific labels for \"Advantages\" and \"Disadvantages\" directly within the Composable, leveraging the `viewModel.appLanguage`. I\'m also doing this to localize descriptions of system guides, like \"Off-Grid System Guidelines,\" which improves component cleanliness.\n\n\n**Elaborating System Descriptions**\n\nI\'m expanding system descriptions for clarity, focusing on the \"Off-Grid System Guidelines\" section. I\'ve added localized strings for different languages, which is more streamlined. I\'m focusing on making them independent of the national power grid, self-sufficient, and powered by solar during the day and batteries at night. These dynamic descriptions, and my work localizing UI elements, are making the system cleaner overall.\n\n\n**Expanding System Advantage Details**\n\nI\'m currently expanding advantage descriptions for off-grid systems, focusing on benefits like independence from the national grid, which includes different language translations. I\'ve now added specific translations for several languages including Bengali, Chinese, German and Korean, which focus on eliminating utility bills and serving areas without an existing power grid. I believe this makes the descriptions clearer.\n\n\n**Detailing System Disadvantages**\n\nI am now focusing on translating the disadvantages associated with off-grid solar systems into multiple languages. I\'m adding Bengali, Chinese, German, and Korean translations to the disadvantages, related to the cost of the initial setup and challenges that arise during periods of heavy cloud cover or rain.\n\n\n**Expanding On-Grid Details**\n\nI\'m now integrating on-grid system details, ensuring title and descriptions are accurately localized. I\'ve translated the on-grid title to Bengali, Chinese, German and Korean. Furthermore, I\'ve started the on-grid description translations, beginning with Bengali, and I am excited to continue the effort.\n\n\n**Adding On-Grid Advantages**\n\nI\'m now focusing on on-grid advantages. I have added descriptions related to cost-effectiveness, with Bengali, Chinese, German, and Korean translations. I am also planning to include further details regarding the advantages to the system.\n\n\n**Adding On-Grid Advantages**\n\nI\'ve added further on-grid advantage details, expanding upon cost-effectiveness. Specifically, I included translations for \"no yearly costs associated with battery degradation,\" which focuses on the absence of battery-related expenses. These translations are included in Bengali, Chinese, German and Korean.\n\n\n**Translating On-Grid Disadvantages**\n\nI\'m now working on the on-grid disadvantages. I have focused on translating the disadvantage details associated with on-grid systems in multiple languages, including Bengali, Chinese, German, and Korean. Currently, I\'m integrating translations for \"no yearly costs associated with battery degradation,\" which focuses on the absence of battery-related expenses. The new translations are for: \"Keine laufenden Kosten f\303\274r Batterieverschlei\303\237,\" \"\353\260\260\355\204\260\353\246\254 \354\210\230\353\252\205 \354\240\200\355\225\230 \353\260\217 \352\265\220\354\262\264\354\227\220 \353\224\260\353\245\270 \353\271\204\354\232\251\354\235\264 \354\227\206\354\212\265\353\213\210\353\213\244.,\" and \"Zero recurrent cost of battery pack replacements over time.\" Additionally, I\'m handling the automatically shutdown feature in cases of power outage, translating for multiple languages as well.\n\n\n**Integrating Hybrid Descriptions**\n\nI\'m now integrating hybrid system details, focusing on title and description localization. I\'ve added translations for the hybrid title in Bengali, Chinese, German, and Korean.  I\'ve started the hybrid description translations, beginning with Bengali, and will continue with this.\n\n\n**Defining Hybrid Benefits**\n\nI\'m translating the hybrid system advantages, adding Bengali, Chinese, German, and Korean translations. The focus is on combining on-grid and off-grid benefits, sharing power with the grid, and battery backup during outages. This expansion is making it clearer to users.\n\n\n**Adding Hybrid Disadvantages**\n\nI am now focusing on hybrid system disadvantages. I am adding multiple language translations for drawbacks, including the potential for initial costs. I\'ve translated to Bengali, Chinese, German and Korean the initial costs and maintenance drawbacks.\n\n\n\n**Refining Hybrid Advantage Details**\n\nI\'m currently refining the hybrid system advantage descriptions. I\'ve now integrated translations focusing on the \"most reliable and versatile solar technology.\" These are translated for Bengali, Chinese, German and Korean.\n\n\n**Defining Guide Header Translations**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the translation strings for the guide headers within the `SolarGridGuideTab`. I\'ve defined language-specific labels for the guide header and sub-header. I have added translations for Bengali, Chinese, German and Korean, and am making sure they are displayed dynamically based on the `viewModel.appLanguage` selection.\n\n\n**Optimizing Guideline Translations**\n\nI\'m now working on optimizing and expanding the translation strings for system guidelines within the SolarGridGuideTab. I\'ve focused on translating the headers and sub-headers. I\'ve translated headers in Bengali, Chinese, German and Korean, ensuring dynamic display based on the selected app language. This included inverter sizing and engineering guidelines.\n\n\n**Expanding Inverter Translations**\n\nI\'m now expanding inverter capacity and surge capacity translations to four languages. I\'m focusing on \"Minimum Capacity\" and \"Minimum Surge Power (10s)\" to ensure accurate translations, including Bengali, Chinese, German and Korean. These key details now appear accurately in the UI.\n\n\n\n**Finalizing Cable Translations**\n\nI\'m now incorporating final cable translations. Specifically, I translated \"Cabling & Safety Specifications\" and \"Maximum Load Current\" into Bengali, Chinese, German and Korean. These cable details now appear accurately in the UI.\n\n\n\n**Adding Current Details**\n\nI\'ve just added translations for \"Maximum Continuous Current\" and \"Startup Peak Surge Current\" in Bengali, Chinese, German, and Korean. I\'ve also incorporated translations for the \"Recommended DC Cable\" into the same languages. These translations significantly enhance the usability of the app by presenting crucial electrical specifications in multiple languages.\n\n\n**Adding Fuse Details**\n\nI\'ve just added translations for \"Recommended Safety Fuse (DC Fuse)\" and incorporated translations for \"Solar Panel Sizing\" details in Bengali, Chinese, German, and Korean. These translations help users find the precise recommended fuse size and better understand solar panel requirements.\n\n\n**Expanding Panel Sizing Details**\n\nI\'ve just focused on translating solar panel sizing guidelines, ensuring clarity across languages. I have begun the task of ensuring that I incorporate Bengali, Chinese, German and Korean translations for these sizing details, focusing on accurate descriptions for panel requirements to recharge a battery in 5 hours of sunlight. I have also begun integrating translations to guide users to determine the exact solar panel sizing.\n\n\n**Expanding Panel Sizing Details**\n\nI\'ve just focused on translating the solar panel sizing guidelines, which is making the app clearer to users. I\'ve incorporated Bengali, Chinese, German and Korean translations, and have accurately described panel requirements to recharge a battery within 5 hours of sunlight. I\'m also helping users determine the exact solar panel sizing.\n\n\n"
