    thinking: "**Considering Copyright Display**\n\nI\'ve been thinking about the copyright. I\'ve concluded that we don\'t necessarily need to localize it. Tanzir Ahmed\'s copyright can be presented in Bengali and English, or nicely formatted in both. Right now, I\'m leaning toward displaying the information bilingually.\n\n\n**Designing Legal UI**\n\nI\'ve decided on a polished \"Copyright & Legal Notice Dialog.\" I envision it triggered by a \"Gavel\" or \"Info\" icon in the `CenterAlignedTopAppBar`. The goal is to make it appear official and clear, using an intuitive UI. I am currently examining the `CenterAlignedTopAppBar` component in the `BatteryCalculatorScreen.kt` file.\n\n\n**Adding Copyright Icon**\n\nI\'ve been exploring how to integrate the copyright information into the UI. I believe adding a new icon within the `actions` section of the `CenterAlignedTopAppBar` is the right approach, perhaps using `Icons.Default.VerifiedUser` or `Icons.Default.Gavel`. This icon would trigger the copyright dialog, making it easily accessible.\n\n\n**Refining Icon Selection**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the best icon for the legal notice. After considering several options, including `Icons.Default.Info`, `Icons.Default.Security`, and `Icons.Default.VerifiedUser`, I\'m leaning heavily towards either `Icons.Default.Security` or `Icons.Default.VerifiedUser` due to their associations with security, authenticity, and legal verification, and since I verified that both options are included within the standard Material Icons set. I\'m also considering adding a persistent footer or card within the \"Saved Designs\" tab at the bottom of the scroll.\n\n\n**Exploring UI Placement**\n\nI\'m now thinking about broader UI placement. I love the \"Info/Copyright & Legal Warning\" card idea at the bottom of scrolls in tabs other than \"Saved Systems.\" I\'m now looking at integrating the card at the bottom of the `SavedSystemsTab` and `SolarGridGuideTab`. I\'ll also retain the legal icon in the top app bar for dialog display. I want this to be both easily accessible and visually consistent across the application. I am thinking of including the legal notice and the legal text provided in the design.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will view the end of `BatteryCalculatorScreen.kt` to understand how helper composables are structured and locate the perfect insertion point for the copyright components."
