  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Capacity Conversion**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the feasibility of a unit conversion utility for battery capacity measurements. I need to understand which units are most relevant and commonly used in battery technology. This includes considering different standards and potential user needs within the battery field.\n\n\n**Developing Unit Converter & Components**\n\nI\'ve been iterating on the idea of a simple unit converter, perhaps integrated as a dedicated section or dialog within the application, alongside an interactive component tailored to calculating total energy for LFP batteries. This involves taking into account Ampere-hours and nominal voltage. I\'m also planning a chart component that visualizes a standard LFP battery discharge curve; and am considering both a charting library or drawing the chart with Canvas.\n\n\n**Evaluating Charting Alternatives**\n\nI\'m now comparing charting libraries versus a custom Canvas chart implementation for the LFP discharge curve. The instructions favor a library, but I\'m leaning toward Canvas due to its reliability, customizability, and adherence to guidelines. I\'m focusing on evaluating the existing project environment, checking for existing dependencies in `app/build.gradle.kts` and reviewing the skill check to ensure all relevant skills are utilized.\n\n\n**Assessing Skill Relevance**\n\nI\'m now cross-referencing my skill set against the project requirements. Most skills, like Android CLI and secret management, are irrelevant. Frontend design, which I reviewed earlier, remains pertinent. I\'m focusing on ensuring I leverage my appropriate existing skills and identifying any gaps.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will first inspect `/app/build.gradle.kts` to understand the current configuration and included dependencies."
