  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Planning User Requirements**\n\nI\'ve been examining the code\'s clean approach to localization, especially how `BatteryLocalizer.get(key, lang)` dynamically handles different languages, currently \"en\", \"bn\", \"zh\", \"de\", \"ko\" etc. Now, I\'m focusing on dissecting three user requirements to develop an interactive and well-integrated solution for the application.\n\n\n**Designing Unit Conversion**\n\nI\'m now deep-diving into the first user requirement. I\'m focusing on a unit conversion utility, specifically its interactive design. I\'m imagining a clean, visual card with clear inputs and outputs for battery-related measurements. The interface will let users choose \"From\" and \"To\" units, input the value, and specify voltage (crucial for Ah/Wh conversions). Real-time updates and error handling are key priorities. I\'ve pinpointed units to include: Ah, Wh, kWh, Joules, MJ, and BTU.\n\n\n**Developing LFP Tools**\n\nI\'m now expanding the application\'s utility with an \"LFP Pro Tools\" tab in the main navigation (Tab index 4). I\'m focusing on the \"LFP Energy Calculator\" within this tab, which will compute total energy (Wh/kWh) using Ah and Voltage inputs. I\'m prioritizing user-friendliness with both slider and keyboard input options for Ah capacity and nominal voltage. I\'m also including a crucial Series/Parallel multiplier with S and P count inputs. The live display will feature Total Pack Nominal Voltage, Total Pack Ah capacity, Total Pack Energy in Wh and kWh, and equivalent energy in Lead-Acid.\n\n\n**Adding Visualizations**\n\nI\'m now integrating an interactive visualization component within the new \"LFP Pro Tools\" tab. I\'m focusing on a voltage discharge curve chart, displayed right next to the energy calculator, so it\'s beautifully contained together. I\'m planning a custom-drawn Canvas chart depicting the standard LFP battery discharge characteristics: three stages: initial drop, flat plateau, and the final drop. The goal is to provide a visually clear and educational representation for the user.\n\n\n"
