to align an `Icon` and `Text` for clarity and visual appeal. I\'m currently structuring the callback logic for the inputs.\n\n\n**Defining Input Field Styles**\n\nI\'m now styling the input field elements within the `LfpEnergyCalculatorCard`. I\'m focusing on ensuring visual consistency using `MaterialTheme.colorScheme.primary` for section headers, and utilizing `MaterialTheme.typography.bodySmall` with `onSurfaceVariant` color for descriptive text. I\'ve incorporated an `HorizontalDivider` to separate elements, and am now setting up the `Column` with the `Text` \"cell_capacity_ah\" and a spacer for separation. I am setting up `OutlinedTextField` as the input field.\n\n\n**Styling the Ah Input**\n\nI\'m now implementing the `OutlinedTextField` for the Ah input, ensuring it\'s aesthetically pleasing. I\'ve configured a \"Ah\" suffix to provide clarity, using appropriate colors and visual spacing. I\'m focusing on incorporating suggestion chips to allow the user to conveniently select common preset values, and I am dynamically styling the suggestions with `primaryContainer` based on whether each preset has been selected.\n\n\n**Configuring Nominal Voltage**\n\nI\'m now integrating the nominal cell voltage input. I\'m leveraging `OutlinedTextField` for this. I\'ve successfully added a \"V\" suffix for clarity, and implemented robust input validation. I\'m focusing on user-friendliness with `Number` keyboard input, and now setting up a dynamic display.\n\n\n**Adding Voltage Presets**\n\nI\'m now incorporating intuitive preset buttons to modify both the nominal voltage and the number of series cells. I\'ve designed these to enable quick selections for standard configurations, such as cell level, 12V, 24V, and 48V systems. I\'m focusing on ensuring these presets offer a streamlined and user-friendly experience, while maintaining the overall layout\'s integrity. I am now incorporating these presets.\n\n\n**Implementing the Preset Chip**\n\nI\'m now refining the preset chip