nverter. I\'ve successfully incorporated the conversion logic and displayed the results. I\'m focusing on ensuring data integrity and user-friendliness across the feature. The conversion now handles different input types, including decimal numbers.\n\n\n**Adding Conversion Logic**\n\nI\'m now integrating the core conversion logic, and I\'ve added error handling. I\'m dynamically displaying the conversion results and now adding a nominal system voltage. The voltage is required if either \'From\' or \'To\' units are Amp-hours.\n\n\n**Adjusting the Conversion Display**\n\nI\'m now refining the display of converted results. I\'ve integrated a `Divider` for clearer visual separation and am formatting the results based on the target unit, ensuring precision. I\'m dynamically updating the results based on the target conversion. I am making the results section\'s background, and then I will finalize the styles.\n\n\\n\\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in refining the presentation of the conversion output, making sure it is clear and easy to understand. I\'m focusing on handling different numerical formats for various units, including displaying decimal numbers correctly. I\'m using the provided code for the format. I will now integrate the nominal system voltage.\n\n\n**Designing the Discharge Curve**\n\nI\'m now fully focused on the design of the `LfpDischargeCurveCard`, the next major UI component. I\'m focusing on creating an elegant and informative custom canvas drawing of the discharge curve for LFP batteries. I\'ll need to define horizontal lines for voltage grid. I\'m implementing interactive drag or touch functionality to track `touchSoC` within a range.\n\n\n**Implementing the Discharge Curve**\n\nI\'m now implementing the drawing of the discharge curve, focusing on the visual representation of voltage over State of Charge. I\'m leveraging a `Path` for the discharge curve and implementing a `CustomCanvas` drawing. The code is clean. I am focusing on the drawing logic, with a grid and voltage display. I will now integrate interactive touch to track the SoC.\n\n\n**Enhancing the Discharge Curve**\n\nI am now adding aesthetic improvements to the discharge curve. I\'m focusing on incorporating a filled, semi-transparent gradient beneath the curve to give it a modern and polished look. I will then integrate the touch and drag functionality to enhance user interaction and interactivity.\n\n\n\n**Implementing Touch Functionality**\n\nI\'m now integrating touch interaction into the discharge curve, allowing precise SoC tracking. I\'m focusing on responsiveness by using `detectDragGestures` for seamless drag and touch events. I\'m calculating touch coordinates relative to the graph and now integrating `drawContext` to draw the graph with grid and labels.\n\n\n**Adding Native Canvas Text**\n\nI\'m now integrating the native `android.graphics.Paint` for text rendering on the discharge curve\'s canvas, ensuring optimal performance and compatibility. I\'ve imported `android.graphics.Paint` and `android.graphics.Typeface` to streamline this, and will create clean text labels within the drawing logic. I can draw the axis labels accurately.\n\n\n"
