    modified_response: "I have successfully designed and built the complete suite of **LFP Pro Tools** within the application. Every feature has been crafted with Material Design 3 guidelines, supporting real-time reactivity, fully responsive interaction on the custom canvas chart, and bilingual support (English and Bengali).\n\n### \360\237\233\240\357\270\217 Summary of Accomplishments\n\n1. **LFP Energy & Configuration Calculator**:\n   - Calculates the total pack energy by multiplying Cell Capacity (Ah), Nominal Cell Voltage (V), and custom series (S) and parallel (P) configurations.\n   - Includes standard prismatic/cylindrical cell capacity presets (50Ah, 100Ah, 200Ah, 280Ah, 304Ah) and standard system voltages (3.2V cell, 12.8V 4S, 25.6V 8S, 51.2V 16S).\n   - Features a **Lead-Acid Equivalency Advantage Analysis**, which explains that due to LFP\'s high usable Depth of Discharge (DoD) compared to Lead-Acid\'s restrictive 50% limit, a Lead-Acid pack must be twice the size to provide the equivalent usable energy in real-world scenarios.\n\n2. **Bilingual Unit Capacity Converter Utility**:\n   - Allows users to toggle between different capacity measurements commonly used in battery tech: **Ah**, **Wh**, **kWh**, **Joules (J)**, **MegaJoules (MJ)**, and **British Thermal Units (BTU)**.\n   - Intelligently detects when **Ah** is selected as either the source or destination, dynamically presenting a field for the system\'s nominal voltage (since physical conversion between current-capacity and energy-capacity requires the voltage reference).\n\n3. **Interactive LFP Voltage Discharge Curve**:\n   - Created a custom native **Jetpack Compose Canvas** chart simulating standard LiFePO4 cell discharge profiles (capturing the signature flat 3.2V plateau between 10% and 90% SoC, and the upper/lower sharp knees).\n   - Equipped with **touch gesture tracking** so that dragging your finger across the graph draws a dynamic crosshair with a pulsing node and displays real-time statistics: **SoC (%)**, **Cell Voltage (V)**, and **Total Pack Voltage (V)** (linked dynamically to the series count currently set in your calculator).\n"
