  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing APK Download Center**\n\nI\'m focusing on crafting a fantastic \"APK Download & Installation Center\" card. My plan is to integrate it seamlessly within both the `DeveloperCopyrightSection()` (Tab 4) and the `showCopyrightDialog` (triggered by the Gavel icon). Now I\'m pausing to take a closer look and ensure I\'m making the right choices.\n\n\n**Defining UI Elements**\n\nNow, I\'m defining the UI elements for the \"APK Download & Installation Center.\" I want a prominent title with an Android icon (ideally `Icons.Default.Android`). If unavailable, I\'ll use `Icons.Default.GetApp` or `Icons.Default.FileDownload`. I\'m also including clear buttons: one for downloading the Live Web App (PWA) and another linking to Tanzir\'s GitHub repository. Finally, I\'ll integrate step-by-step instructions for generating the APK within the Google AI Studio menu.\n\n\n**Refactoring into a Composable**\n\nI\'ve refactored the APK download section. Instead of embedding, I\'ve created a reusable `ApkDownloadSection` composable function for better cleanliness. This includes a `Card` container, a `Column` for layout, and a `Row` for the download icon. The composable leverages `LocalUriHandler` for handling external links and adopts a theme-aware design with colors and a border. I\'ve chosen `Icons.Default.FileDownload` for the download icon.\n\n\n**Translating the UI**\n\nI\'m now translating the UI elements. I\'ve switched the title to Bengali, crafting a localized title, \"\340\246\205\340\247\215\340\246\257\340\246\276\340\246\250\340\247\215\340\246\241\340\247\215\340\246\260\340\246\257\340\246\274\340\247\207\340\246\241 APK \340\246\241\340\246\276\340\246\211\340\246\250\340\246\262\340\247\213\340\246\241 \340\246\223 \340\246\207\340\246\250\340\246\270\340\247\215\340\246\237\340\246\262\340\247\207\340\246\266\340\246\250 \340\246\227\340\246\276\340\246\207\340\246\241,\" complete with an Android icon and bold emphasis. Below the title is the introductory text \"\340\246\205\340\247\215\340\246\257\340\246\276\340\246\252\340\246\237\340\246\277 \340\246\270\340\246\260\340\246\276\340\246\270\340\246\260\340\246\277 \340\246\206\340\246\252\340\246\250\340\246\276\340\246\260 \340\246\205\340\247\215\340\246\257\340\246\276\340\246\250\340\247\215\340\246\241\340\247\215\340\246\260\340\246\257\340\246\274\340\247\207\340\246\241 \340\246\253\340\247\213\340\246\250\340\247\207 \340\246\207\340\246\250\340\246\270\340\247\215\340\246\237\340\246\262 \340\246\225\340\246\260\340\247\207 \340\246\254\340\247\215\340\246\257\340\246\254\340\246\271\340\246\276\340\246\260\340\247\207\340\246\260 \340\246\234\340\246\250\340\247\215\340\246\257 \340\246\250\340\246\277\340\246\232\340\247\207\340\246\260 \340\246\247\340\246\276\340\246\252\340\246\227\340\247\201\340\246\262\340\247\213 \340\246\205\340\246\250\340\247\201\340\246\270\340\246\260\340\246\243 \340\246\225\340\246\260\340\247\201\340\246\250:\" The step-by-step guidance is about to be displayed in a column with rounded corners.\n\n\n**Adding Bengali Steps**\n\nI\'ve added the Bengali step-by-step instructions for APK generation within the composable. I translated the steps into Bengali: click the Settings or Export menu in the upper right corner of Google AI Studio, choose \"Generate APK\" or \"Download ZIP,\" and then download and install the .apk file. Now I\'m working on the design.\n\n\n**Integrating Buttons**\n\nI\'m integrating two buttons now. One is a primary-colored button linking directly to the Live Web App (PWA) using `Icons.Default.Language`. The other, an outlined button, directs to Tanzir\'s GitHub with `Icons.Default.Code`. These buttons are now arranged spaced by 8.dp to offer a good user experience.\n\n\n**Verifying Icon Imports**\n\nI\'m verifying the icon imports. I confirmed `Icons.Default.FileDownload` and `Icons.Default.Code` are present in `androidx.compose.material.icons.filled.*`. I\'m now double-checking standard alternatives like `Icons.Default.GetApp` or `Icons.Default.ArrowDownward` to ensure maximum compatibility and avoid any potential issues. I\'ve decided to use `Icons.Default.GetApp` and `Icons.Default.Code` for the best outcome. I am also checking the location of `DeveloperCopyrightSection()` in `BatteryCalculatorScreen.kt`.\n\n\n**Positioning the Section**\n\nMy latest thought is on placement! I\'ve decided to put the `ApkDownloadSection()` right above `DeveloperCopyrightSection()`. I\'ll also render it in both `DeveloperCopyrightSection` and `showCopyrightDialog`. I\'m now examining the structure of `showCopyrightDialog` (lines 340-430) to ensure seamless integration.\n\n\n**Refining Copyright Section**\n\nI am now focusing on refining the copyright section. I\'ve been reviewing the layout and content. I\'ve re-examined the code. I am thinking of updating the copy. I want to improve readability. I\'ve added a visual separator. I\'m aiming for clarity in both Bengali and English.\n\n\n**Improving Copyright Content**\n\nI am currently working on the copyright section. I am streamlining the \"Developer & Owner\" section. I\'ve considered formatting changes to boost visual appeal. I\'ve re-written the developer\'s name and GitHub link for improved flow and aesthetics, focusing on clarity.\n\n\n**Integrating Section Now**\n\nI\'m now integrating the `ApkDownloadSection()` into the `showCopyrightDialog`. I\'ve identified the insertion point after the copyright text and a separator, right before the concluding text section. I\'m focusing on ensuring it\'s positioned correctly and maintains the intended visual flow. I\'m double-checking the code to avoid any layout conflicts.\n\n\n"
